        </p>
        <p>
            <label for="<?php echo $this->get_field_id('content'); ?>"><?php _e( 'Content:' ); ?></label>
            <textarea class="widefat" id="<?php echo $this->get_field_id('content'); ?>" name="<?php echo $this->get_field_name('content'); ?>"><?php echo esc_attr($content); ?></textarea>
        </p>
        <?php
    }

    // sanitization function
    function update($new_instance, $old_instance) {
        $instance = array();
        $instance['title'] = strip_tags($new_instance['title']);
        $instance['content'] = strip_tags($new_instance['content']);
        return $instance;
    }
}
```

in the code snippet above, you can customize the widget's name, description, width, and form fields to fit your needs.

