- `is_empty()` returns True if the queue is empty, False otherwise.
- `enqueue(value)` adds a new node with the given value at the tail of the list.
- `dequeue()` removes the node at the head of the list and returns its value.
- `see_saw()` iterates through the nodes in the middle of the list to compute the required sum.

The time complexity of each operation is O(1), as required, and the space complexity is O(n), where n is the current size of the queue. Note that the see_saw() operation has a hidden multiplicative constant factor for the computation of fractions (1 / current_node.prev.value), but this is still O(1) on average.

